planningNotes.codebaseInsights:
Architect measurements, 2026-10-31, native Windows driven from WSL (pwsh 7.6.9 Store install, PS 5.1, Windows node 24.16, Git 2.54):
- The CI-style chain pwsh -> node -> powershell.exe 5.1 'wrapper' -> node guard -> powershell.exe fails on HEAD as well. Even Get-Acl in the 5.1 wrapper itself fails with CouldNotAutoloadMatchingModule. CI's Windows legs (a pwsh step running node) are therefore hit by the same bug, and the same fix covers them.
- Under pwsh -> node -> powershell.exe:
  - postflight.{sh,ps1}'s leak probe (Get-CimInstance plus ConvertTo-Json) exits 0;
  - local-runner probeHypervisor (Get-CimInstance) exits 0;
  - agent-git-guard.test.mjs's own Get-Acl check exits 1;
  - [IO.Directory]::GetAccessControl exits 0.
- The guard dirs the patched program created report AreAccessRulesProtected=True.
- In the launchers, the only powershell.exe spawn is this ACL step: one in each twin, byte-identical (56-line program).
- node:test TAP prints '# skipped 0', not '# skip'.
- A prototype of exactly this plan gave:
  - Linux 25/25 (57 s);
  - Windows 26/26 with 0 skipped (152 s);
  - acceptance.test.ts natively: RED on HEAD ('lands once...' fails with MOE_AGENT_GIT_GUARD_FAILED), 6/6 GREEN with the fix (15 s);
  - postflight.ps1 under pwsh 7 with the fix: PASS through scenario Z (1176 s).
